-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Indonesia Family Life Survey (IFLS): Study design and results from waves 1 and 2</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>RAND Corporation, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greene</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><source>Econometric analysis</source><year>1997</year><edition>3</edition><publisher-name>Prentice-Hall: Englewood Cliffs NJ</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yip</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determinants of patient choice of medical provider: a case study in rural China</article-title><source>Health Policy and Planning</source><year>1998</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10187600</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/heapol/13.3.311</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Stata Corporation</collab></person-group><source>Stata statistical software Release 70</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Texas: College Station</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thabrany</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pujianto</surname><given-names/></name></person-group><article-title>Health Insurance and access to health care</article-title><source>The Journal of the Indonesian Medical Association</source><year>2000</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>282</fpage><lpage>289</lpage></citation></ref><ref i